(D2 - Discrepancy 2 repro: LANGUAGE.md:139 says a blank line force-closes
 EVERY open clause at once, including an enclosing function definition,
 and LANGUAGE.md:91 says the blank line is what closes a function body.
 An `Otherwise` after that blank line nonetheless continues the `if`
 inside the function - it prints the parameter `n`, so it is executing
 inside `check`'s frame.
 An intervening statement does end the chain: moving `Print "between".`
 above the `Otherwise` turns it into
   error: Expected a statement, got Otherwise
 So the chain is ended by a statement but not by a paragraph break.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   other 2
   done
)
